  "journal": {
    "s17_journal": {
      "title": "Six Histories, One Mystery",
      "text": "All six kingdoms came to Valebridge, and all six fragments fit the table, except for an empty space in the middle. Each kingdom remembered a different part: a foundation, a boundary, a marker, a warning, a sealed inheritance. Under Orin's light, writing showed in the grooves: the people who built before the crowns left it to six keepers and told them never to open the door. The Ancient Builders made the gateway; we only inherited the pieces. The spiral gives the way in, beneath the monument's eastern foundation. At dawn the joint expedition sets out."
    }
  }
